WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.726
Can a bill become law if

2
00:00:01.726 --> 00:00:03.386
the Rajya Sabha rejects it?

3
00:00:03.686 --> 00:00:05.563
For an ordinary bill, yes.

4
00:00:06.063 --> 00:00:07.791
A bill must pass both Houses,

5
00:00:07.891 --> 00:00:09.491
then get the President's assent.

6
00:00:09.941 --> 00:00:11.413
If one House rejects it,

7
00:00:11.513 --> 00:00:12.861
if they finally disagree

8
00:00:12.861 --> 00:00:13.647
on amendments,

9
00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:15.133
or if six months pass,

10
00:00:15.283 --> 00:00:16.576
the President can call a

11
00:00:16.576 --> 00:00:17.331
joint sitting.

12
00:00:17.781 --> 00:00:19.523
There, a majority of members

13
00:00:19.523 --> 00:00:21.202
of both Houses, present and

14
00:00:21.202 --> 00:00:22.197
voting, decides.

15
00:00:22.647 --> 00:00:24.418
It never applies to a Money Bill,

16
00:00:24.538 --> 00:00:26.298
and constitutional amendments

17
00:00:26.298 --> 00:00:27.269
can't go to one.

18
00:00:27.719 --> 00:00:29.532
It has happened only three times:

19
00:00:29.652 --> 00:00:33.556
in 1961, 1978 and 2002.

20
00:00:34.006 --> 00:00:35.073
Two Houses.

21
00:00:35.273 --> 00:00:36.937
One way out of a deadlock.

22
00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:38.333
Your turn.

23
00:00:38.633 --> 00:00:39.980
Which bill can never go to

24
00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:40.809
a joint sitting?
